      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Various preparations of botulinum toxin type A (BTX-A) are used to reduces glabellar (frown) lines. However, dose-related safety and efficacy of intramuscular injections of a widely used, locally produced BTX-A in China has not been established."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "Assessment of dose-dependent safety and efficacy of Chinese botulinum toxin type A (Hengli BTX-A [HBTX-A]) intramuscular injections on glabellar lines."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Four hundred eighty-eight BTX-A-naive participants were included in the double-blind trial and randomly divided into placebo (n = 122), low-dose (n = 183), and high-dose (n = 183) treatment groups for injection with saline solution, 10 units and 20 units of HBTX-A, respectively, at 4 sites in the corrugator muscle and 1 site in the procerus muscle. Outcomes were recorded before treatment and after 7, 30, 60, and 120 days, including glabellar line severity at maximum contraction and relaxation."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Significantly greater improvement was observed in both HBTX-A groups in comparison with the placebo group (p < .05). Better efficacy was obtained in the high-dose treatment group. More participants developed adverse events after treatment with HBTX-A doses, than with the placebo (p < .05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Twenty-unit HBTX-A provided optimal improvement in glabellar lines, and its use might minimize injection frequency while maintaining acceptable safety."
        }
      ]},
